# Azure Data Explorer MCP Server Configuration

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED: Azure Data Explorer Configuration
# ============================================================================
ADX_CLUSTER_URL=https://your-cluster.region.kusto.windows.net
ADX_DATABASE=YourDatabaseName

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED: MCP Server Configuration
# ============================================================================
ADX_MCP_SERVER_TRANSPORT=http
ADX_MCP_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0
ADX_MCP_BIND_PORT=3000

# ============================================================================
# AUTHENTICATION: Service Principal with Client Secret (RECOMMENDED)
# ============================================================================
# To use Service Principal authentication, set all three values below:
AZURE_TENANT_ID=your-tenant-id-here
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here

# How to get these values:
# 1. Go to Azure Portal → Azure Active Directory → App registrations
# 2. Find or create your Service Principal (App Registration)
# 3. AZURE_TENANT_ID: Copy "Directory (tenant) ID" from Overview
# 4. AZURE_CLIENT_ID: Copy "Application (client) ID" from Overview
# 5. AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET: Go to "Certificates & secrets" → "New client secret"
#    - Create a new secret and copy its value immediately
#    - Note: The secret value is only shown once!

# ============================================================================
# AUTHENTICATION: Workload Identity (Kubernetes only)
# ============================================================================
# If running in Kubernetes with Workload Identity, set only:
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=your-tenant-id
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
# ADX_TOKEN_FILE_PATH=/var/run/secrets/azure/tokens/azure-identity-token

# ============================================================================
# AUTHENTICATION: Default Azure Credential (Fallback)
# ============================================================================
# If none of the above are set, the server will use DefaultAzureCredential
# which tries: Managed Identity → Azure CLI → Visual Studio Code, etc.

# ============================================================================
# PERMISSIONS REQUIRED
# ============================================================================
# Your Service Principal needs the following permissions on ADX:
# - Database Viewer (or higher) on the target database
# 
# To grant permissions in ADX:
# .add database YourDatabaseName viewers ('aadapp=YOUR_CLIENT_ID;YOUR_TENANT_ID')
